1
00:00:58,413 --> 00:01:00,624
Previously on Dating Alys Perez.

2
00:01:00,649 --> 00:01:02,651
Would you tell your wife

3
00:01:02,651 --> 00:01:05,028
that I'm not here to be her best friend.

4
00:01:05,028 --> 00:01:06,421
Fier is pregnant.

5
00:01:07,322 --> 00:01:09,240
It's not like I can ask her to leave.

6
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:10,784
She’s carrying my grandchild.

7
00:01:10,784 --> 00:01:12,827
We both know how
this is going to end.

8
00:01:13,078 --> 00:01:14,621
One of us has to go.

9
00:01:15,038 --> 00:01:16,706
I have a solution, Drake.

10
00:01:16,957 --> 00:01:18,792
I'm leaving.

11
00:01:18,792 --> 00:01:22,879
I haven't a clue as to why
you're tolerating this bullshit!

12
00:01:22,879 --> 00:01:24,714
You're the wife!

13
00:01:24,714 --> 00:01:26,466
Why do you have to leave?

14
00:01:26,591 --> 00:01:28,259
Sometimes I wonder,

15
00:01:29,302 --> 00:01:30,637
why Drake?

16
00:01:31,012 --> 00:01:32,430
Why not just me?

17
00:01:32,430 --> 00:01:33,640
I’m way more handsome, anyway.

18
00:01:34,015 --> 00:01:35,225
- I love you.
- I love you.

19
00:02:04,295 --> 00:02:05,505
Drake?

20
00:02:15,849 --> 00:02:17,058
Oh, right.

21
00:02:17,308 --> 00:02:19,519
When did he ever leave me a note?

22
00:02:19,561 --> 00:02:20,937
I should be used to this.

23
00:02:36,995 --> 00:02:37,912
Hello, Bestie?

24
00:02:37,996 --> 00:02:38,747
Bestie.

25
00:02:38,955 --> 00:02:40,123
Are you at the boutique?

26
00:02:40,415 --> 00:02:41,624
I'll be swinging by.

27
00:02:41,624 --> 00:02:43,251
See you later, bye!

28
00:02:45,761 --> 00:02:47,471
I don't know where Fier went.

29
00:02:49,507 --> 00:02:51,247
Probably at Cristine's.

30
00:02:53,803 --> 00:02:55,055
How'd you know that?

31
00:02:56,056 --> 00:02:58,016
It's the only place she goes.

32
00:02:58,740 --> 00:02:59,991
If she isn't with Drake,

33
00:03:00,611 --> 00:03:02,196
then she must be with Cristine.

34
00:03:02,729 --> 00:03:08,276
Besides, Cristine is the only one who
can put up with her friend’s attitude.

35
00:03:09,998 --> 00:03:11,666
That's harsh.

36
00:03:12,447 --> 00:03:14,532
Why?
It's true.

37
00:03:17,452 --> 00:03:19,204
You know, Bestie,

38
00:03:20,121 --> 00:03:23,166
you really got yourself
into a complicated situation.

39
00:03:24,084 --> 00:03:26,836
I don't know why
you let it get this bad.

40
00:03:28,963 --> 00:03:30,590
What’s your plan?

41
00:03:34,761 --> 00:03:36,262
I'm going to see Fier.

42
00:03:37,597 --> 00:03:39,140
Do you need some backup?

43
00:03:39,682 --> 00:03:40,892
Why? Are you free?

44
00:03:41,217 --> 00:03:43,219
Of course! Just for you.

45
00:03:54,656 --> 00:03:55,465
Why?

46
00:03:55,490 --> 00:03:56,825
There you go.

47
00:03:56,825 --> 00:03:57,992
A message from that creep.

48
00:04:02,832 --> 00:04:04,322
If you ask me, Aya,

49
00:04:05,708 --> 00:04:07,544
we all have our own wars to win.

50
00:04:08,336 --> 00:04:10,130
I can do this on my own.

51
00:04:10,130 --> 00:04:11,798
Face your own battle.

52
00:04:14,551 --> 00:04:17,720
You know, with all of your struggles,

53
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:19,806
you still find time to annoy me.

54
00:04:20,306 --> 00:04:22,934
Oh, come on, Bestie.
I rarely have fun these days.

55
00:04:24,769 --> 00:04:26,104
Jeez.

56
00:05:04,017 --> 00:05:05,268
Are you sure about that?

57
00:05:05,268 --> 00:05:07,061
I already talked to the twins.

58
00:05:07,061 --> 00:05:10,064
They'll be handling
my papers and everything.

59
00:05:10,064 --> 00:05:12,775
I just need to stay here
until I get my ticket.

60
00:05:12,775 --> 00:05:14,611
You really won't tell me what country?

61
00:05:15,195 --> 00:05:17,071
I'm leaving Drake and everything.

62
00:05:17,071 --> 00:05:19,616
And you being his friend
puts me in jeopardy.

63
00:05:20,116 --> 00:05:21,618
It's better that you don’t know.

64
00:05:22,785 --> 00:05:24,329
But I'm your best friend too.

65
00:05:24,329 --> 00:05:25,580
I know.

66
00:05:26,164 --> 00:05:27,498
We can video chat!

67
00:05:27,957 --> 00:05:29,626
That's not fair.

68
00:05:30,168 --> 00:05:32,086
How can I be the
baby's godmother when

69
00:05:32,086 --> 00:05:34,797
I don't even know
where to send my gifts?

70
00:05:36,174 --> 00:05:38,509
You're such a child sometimes, Cristine.

71
00:05:38,509 --> 00:05:40,303
But you'll see my baby, okay?

72
00:05:40,803 --> 00:05:43,139
We'll video chat as frequent as possible.

73
00:05:43,139 --> 00:05:45,099
And maybe after—

74
00:05:45,266 --> 00:05:47,894
Maybe after some years
when everything's okay,

75
00:05:48,728 --> 00:05:50,521
I'll let you know where we are.

76
00:05:51,231 --> 00:05:52,815
When will you leave?

77
00:05:53,483 --> 00:05:54,651
Leave?

78
00:05:55,318 --> 00:05:56,569
Where is she going?

79
00:05:56,736 --> 00:05:57,779
She's leaving Drake?

80
00:05:58,529 --> 00:06:01,074
Is she really going to deny
Drake his rights as a father?

81
00:06:01,783 --> 00:06:03,243
I don't know yet.

82
00:06:03,451 --> 00:06:05,036
Maybe tonight,

83
00:06:05,161 --> 00:06:06,788
tomorrow or next week?

84
00:06:07,372 --> 00:06:09,165
As soon as possible.

85
00:06:09,666 --> 00:06:11,542
Are you sure about this?

86
00:06:12,126 --> 00:06:12,919
Yeah.

87
00:06:13,836 --> 00:06:15,213
My decision is final.

88
00:06:30,937 --> 00:06:32,146
Hi.

89
00:06:32,146 --> 00:06:33,147
Wait!

90
00:06:34,065 --> 00:06:35,858
You again?

91
00:06:36,985 --> 00:06:38,528
Are you Fier's brothers?

92
00:06:38,945 --> 00:06:40,613
Yes, why?

93
00:06:41,030 --> 00:06:41,906
I'm Alys.

94
00:06:42,282 --> 00:06:43,825
Oh!

95
00:06:44,367 --> 00:06:46,327
You're the Alys Perez.

96
00:06:46,995 --> 00:06:48,246
You're really something.

97
00:06:48,246 --> 00:06:49,455
You've got some nerve.

98
00:06:50,206 --> 00:06:51,624
What do you want from us?

99
00:06:52,542 --> 00:06:53,501
Please.

100
00:06:53,501 --> 00:06:55,878
You can't let Fier leave the country.

101
00:06:55,878 --> 00:06:57,505
Breathe, Alys.

102
00:06:57,505 --> 00:06:58,840
Lower your pride.

103
00:06:59,132 --> 00:07:00,925
You know what needs to be done.

104
00:07:01,301 --> 00:07:03,052
Stay calm.

105
00:07:03,678 --> 00:07:05,221
You really are something.

106
00:07:05,847 --> 00:07:07,015
Are you insane?

107
00:07:08,308 --> 00:07:09,475
I'm serious.

108
00:07:10,101 --> 00:07:11,936
Fier can't leave the country.

109
00:07:12,353 --> 00:07:14,230
Please, please!

110
00:07:14,856 --> 00:07:16,649
Chance, I'm going ahead.

111
00:07:17,066 --> 00:07:18,860
Maybe I might say something I’ll regret.

112
00:07:20,695 --> 00:07:22,822
Please, listen to me.

113
00:07:23,573 --> 00:07:25,783
You're just wasting your time, Alys.

114
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:28,286
Fier is stubborn as a rock.

115
00:07:28,286 --> 00:07:31,080
What do I have to do
for you to listen to me?

116
00:07:31,998 --> 00:07:33,828
What am I doing?

117
00:07:34,292 --> 00:07:36,796
I feel like I'm making
a deal with the devil.

118
00:07:38,129 --> 00:07:39,339
Whatever.

119
00:07:39,797 --> 00:07:41,466
As long as Fier
doesn’t leave the country,

120
00:07:41,466 --> 00:07:43,634
and Drake doesn’t lose
his right to their child.

121
00:07:44,594 --> 00:07:46,637
Will you be willing to let go of Drake?

122
00:07:47,221 --> 00:07:48,097
What?!

123
00:07:48,306 --> 00:07:49,307
No!

124
00:07:49,307 --> 00:07:51,559
I would do everything but that.

125
00:07:51,934 --> 00:07:56,731
God knows how much I suffered
to get to this point with Drake.

126
00:07:57,376 --> 00:07:58,877
Then, shut up!

127
00:08:01,778 --> 00:08:03,164
My sister is already leaving,

128
00:08:03,477 --> 00:08:04,603
just to give way.

129
00:08:04,989 --> 00:08:06,240
Yet here you are standing in the way.

130
00:08:06,448 --> 00:08:07,741
That's not my intention at all.

131
00:08:08,284 --> 00:08:09,744
I'm just thinking about the child!

132
00:08:09,813 --> 00:08:11,398
They will never know their father!

133
00:08:12,455 --> 00:08:14,082
It's the 21st Century already, miss.

134
00:08:14,582 --> 00:08:17,377
Fier's child doesn't need a father to live.

135
00:08:21,339 --> 00:08:22,757
This can't happen.

136
00:08:23,530 --> 00:08:24,864
I really need to do something.

137
00:10:38,518 --> 00:10:39,936
Hi!
Is Drake around?

138
00:10:40,228 --> 00:10:41,646
Yes, ma'am.
He's inside.

139
00:10:41,729 --> 00:10:43,731
- Thanks.
- Welcome.

140
00:10:48,611 --> 00:10:52,198
001131.
Unlocked.

141
00:10:53,699 --> 00:10:54,951
Drake?

142
00:10:57,828 --> 00:10:59,080
Drake?

143
00:11:56,721 --> 00:11:59,348
Drake really wants to be
a good father.

144
00:12:00,850 --> 00:12:03,603
And Fier wants to take that away from him.

145
00:12:04,979 --> 00:12:09,775
I need to do something.
I need to stop Fier from leaving.

146
00:12:13,904 --> 00:12:15,865
She can't leave.

147
00:12:31,464 --> 00:12:33,299
Pick up, please.

148
00:12:37,261 --> 00:12:39,096
Damn it, Fier!

149
00:12:40,306 --> 00:12:42,576
Can't you just for once—

150
00:12:44,226 --> 00:12:45,311
Try to cooperate.

151
00:12:45,311 --> 00:12:47,688
You’re not the only one
being affected by this.

152
00:13:08,084 --> 00:13:09,804
Fier, please.

153
00:13:12,546 --> 00:13:13,468
Please.

154
00:13:15,341 --> 00:13:16,733
Please.

155
00:13:41,033 --> 00:13:42,535
Hello, Alys?

156
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:44,370
Hello, Cristine?

157
00:13:44,745 --> 00:13:46,288
Oh my god! Are you okay?

158
00:13:47,867 --> 00:13:49,452
Wait, no. Where are you?

159
00:13:49,667 --> 00:13:50,710
I'm coming to you.

160
00:13:50,710 --> 00:13:51,669
Stay put. Stay put.

161
00:13:51,669 --> 00:13:54,255
No, how's Fier?
I wanna know how Fier is.

162
00:13:55,548 --> 00:13:56,757
Alys...

163
00:13:58,175 --> 00:13:59,301
Come on, Cristine, please.

164
00:13:59,301 --> 00:14:00,428
Please help me.

165
00:14:00,761 --> 00:14:01,887
Please help Drake.

166
00:14:03,472 --> 00:14:05,141
As much as I want to,

167
00:14:05,391 --> 00:14:07,351
I just can't, Alys.

168
00:14:08,394 --> 00:14:09,603
It's her life.

169
00:14:09,603 --> 00:14:11,397
And she's really hurt too.

170
00:14:12,064 --> 00:14:14,358
But what about Drake?

171
00:14:14,984 --> 00:14:16,652
I don't know, Alys.

172
00:14:16,652 --> 00:14:18,863
Cristine, he's your best friend.

173
00:14:19,697 --> 00:14:21,824
I mean I care about Drake like you.

174
00:14:22,199 --> 00:14:24,326
And I talked to Fier. I swear.

175
00:14:24,827 --> 00:14:26,537
But she's made up her mind.

176
00:14:26,537 --> 00:14:27,872
You know, she was really hurt

177
00:14:27,872 --> 00:14:29,665
that Drake chose to let her go

178
00:14:29,665 --> 00:14:31,751
despite the fact that
she's having their child.

179
00:14:34,253 --> 00:14:35,504
It was too much for her.

180
00:14:38,507 --> 00:14:39,800
I'm sorry.

181
00:14:58,611 --> 00:14:59,862
My sister is leaving,

182
00:15:00,404 --> 00:15:01,530
just to give way.

183
00:15:01,822 --> 00:15:03,243
Yet here you are standing in the way.

184
00:15:04,074 --> 00:15:05,701
It's the 21st Century already, miss.

185
00:15:06,202 --> 00:15:08,996
Fier's child doesn't
need a father to live.

186
00:15:09,371 --> 00:15:12,541
It's her life.
And she's really hurt too.

187
00:15:12,541 --> 00:15:14,210
As much as I want to,

188
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:16,420
I just can't, Alys.

189
00:15:36,807 --> 00:15:38,969
I'm gonna fix this, Drake.

190
00:15:41,529 --> 00:15:43,329
I’ll fix this.

191
00:15:46,909 --> 00:15:50,371
Ma’am, the mechanic is
already fixing your car.

192
00:15:50,663 --> 00:15:53,082
But you might not be
able to use it just yet.

193
00:15:53,958 --> 00:15:56,460
He says there’s a
mechanical engine problem.

194
00:15:56,460 --> 00:15:58,504
He'll have to bring it to the garage.

195
00:15:59,088 --> 00:16:04,009
If you'd like, I could have the
company service take you home.

196
00:16:04,009 --> 00:16:05,302
Or I can book you a ride.

197
00:16:05,928 --> 00:16:07,471
No, it's fine. Thank you.

198
00:16:07,805 --> 00:16:09,890
It's a good thing you're still here.

199
00:16:09,890 --> 00:16:11,600
At least you weren't on the road.

200
00:16:11,809 --> 00:16:13,978
Something worse could have happened.

201
00:16:14,353 --> 00:16:15,104
Yeah, I know.

202
00:16:15,104 --> 00:16:16,564
Thank you for your assistance, okay?

203
00:16:16,689 --> 00:16:18,274
Okay, Ma'am. Thank you.

204
00:16:19,066 --> 00:16:21,068
Oh, by the way...

205
00:16:21,277 --> 00:16:22,486
Drake still hasn’t arrived?

206
00:16:23,028 --> 00:16:24,280
Not yet, Ma'am.

207
00:16:25,531 --> 00:16:28,242
Update me when he’s here.

208
00:16:28,242 --> 00:16:29,118
Okay?

209
00:16:29,118 --> 00:16:30,494
Of course, Ma'am.

210
00:16:30,744 --> 00:16:31,537
Thank you.

211
00:16:31,537 --> 00:16:32,913
Another thing!

212
00:16:34,373 --> 00:16:37,501
Could you please make sure he
doesn’t work on an empty stomach?

213
00:16:37,501 --> 00:16:39,336
That man is already stressed enough.

214
00:16:40,379 --> 00:16:41,672
Okay, Ma'am.

215
00:16:41,672 --> 00:16:44,049
He does have a bit of a temper lately.

216
00:16:45,384 --> 00:16:47,052
No matter what,

217
00:16:47,052 --> 00:16:49,221
don't let him work without eating first.

218
00:16:49,221 --> 00:16:51,223
Tell him it's an order from Ms. Alys.

219
00:16:51,891 --> 00:16:52,558
Oh no, Ma'am.

220
00:16:52,558 --> 00:16:56,353
He might get mad at me instead.

221
00:16:56,353 --> 00:16:57,730
But,

222
00:16:57,730 --> 00:16:59,148
I'll let him know.

223
00:16:59,148 --> 00:16:59,732
Thank you.

224
00:16:59,732 --> 00:17:02,359
That man is just way too
stubborn for his own good.

225
00:17:02,359 --> 00:17:03,652
But thank you.

226
00:17:03,652 --> 00:17:05,070
Okay, thank you.

227
00:17:25,507 --> 00:17:27,301
Drake still hasn’t arrived.

228
00:17:31,013 --> 00:17:32,723
Not even a text.

229
00:17:34,642 --> 00:17:37,311
Drake, where are you?

230
00:17:39,188 --> 00:17:42,274
I'm in your office.

231
00:17:47,404 --> 00:17:51,924
Make sure you eat and stay safe, okay?

232
00:17:53,723 --> 00:17:54,974
Are you busy?

233
00:17:57,164 --> 00:17:59,243
Drake, please reply.

234
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:06,090
Zy?

235
00:18:08,133 --> 00:18:09,093
Tripp?

236
00:18:11,095 --> 00:18:12,096
What—

237
00:18:14,723 --> 00:18:15,933
Are you okay?

238
00:18:17,059 --> 00:18:18,018
Tripp...

239
00:18:23,649 --> 00:18:24,608
You okay?

240
00:18:25,359 --> 00:18:26,298
What happened?

241
00:18:28,988 --> 00:18:29,947
One second.

242
00:18:30,197 --> 00:18:31,323
I just need to submit something.

243
00:18:31,323 --> 00:18:32,282
Sit down first.

244
00:18:33,283 --> 00:18:34,228
Wait.

245
00:18:34,827 --> 00:18:35,721
I'll be quick.

246
00:18:38,497 --> 00:18:39,486
Hello.

247
00:18:39,707 --> 00:18:41,875
Kindly hand this over
to the Accounting Department.

248
00:18:57,808 --> 00:18:59,059
What's wrong, Zy?

249
00:18:59,853 --> 00:19:00,861
What happened?

250
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:12,156
Come on.

251
00:19:12,531 --> 00:19:13,741
Let's get out of here.

252
00:19:13,741 --> 00:19:14,922
Come with me.

253
00:19:15,075 --> 00:19:15,909
Come with me.

254
00:19:16,702 --> 00:19:18,662
Let’s go, I’ve got you.

255
00:19:32,134 --> 00:19:33,385
You can cry now.

256
00:19:57,242 --> 00:19:58,619
Zy...

257
00:20:00,412 --> 00:20:02,126
I don’t want to sound rude but...

258
00:20:04,625 --> 00:20:06,251
is crying all you can do?

259
00:20:08,337 --> 00:20:11,715
Sorry, but...

260
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:15,416
I just don’t like seeing
you cry every time.

261
00:20:15,886 --> 00:20:17,054
Especially not over Drake.

262
00:20:17,429 --> 00:20:19,431
It's not Drake's fault!

263
00:20:19,431 --> 00:20:21,350
I don't care, Zy.

264
00:20:21,558 --> 00:20:23,811
The point is you're crying all over again.

265
00:20:26,522 --> 00:20:27,485
Zy...

266
00:20:29,108 --> 00:20:29,942
Tripp!

267
00:20:29,942 --> 00:20:30,734
Listen, Zy.

268
00:20:31,401 --> 00:20:32,820
Remember when I said

269
00:20:32,820 --> 00:20:34,238
it's normal to get hurt?

270
00:20:35,072 --> 00:20:36,932
That it's normal to cry in relationships?

271
00:20:38,117 --> 00:20:39,201
But, Zy...

272
00:20:40,661 --> 00:20:42,621
At this point, you're just being a fool.

273
00:20:43,705 --> 00:20:44,998
Come on, Tripp.

274
00:20:49,878 --> 00:20:51,493
I know you love Drake.

275
00:20:53,882 --> 00:20:55,634
And I know he loves you too.

276
00:20:56,468 --> 00:20:57,556
But...

277
00:20:59,285 --> 00:21:01,368
it’s the same thing
over and over again, Zy.

278
00:21:01,598 --> 00:21:02,808
It's unhealthy.

279
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:05,769
This isn’t right anymore.

280
00:21:07,729 --> 00:21:11,483
But I love him, Tripp.

281
00:21:12,109 --> 00:21:13,777
I love him.

282
00:21:14,486 --> 00:21:16,155
We're already married.

283
00:21:16,655 --> 00:21:17,656
Zy,

284
00:21:18,115 --> 00:21:19,366
a marriage...

285
00:21:20,492 --> 00:21:23,328
doesn't end after saying “I do”.

286
00:21:23,453 --> 00:21:26,206
Meaning, every day of your entire life,

287
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:28,750
you chose that person.

288
00:21:30,419 --> 00:21:32,379
But look at what’s
happening to you every day?

289
00:21:32,814 --> 00:21:34,482
You keep on crying.

290
00:21:35,465 --> 00:21:36,967
Is that the life you want?

291
00:21:37,968 --> 00:21:40,387
To cry every day,
because of Drake?

292
00:21:58,155 --> 00:21:59,531
I'm sorry, Alys.

293
00:22:00,407 --> 00:22:02,117
I didn't mean it that way, but...

294
00:22:02,826 --> 00:22:05,454
I hate seeing you cry.
I just want you to be happy, Zy.

295
00:22:06,663 --> 00:22:07,706
That's it.

296
00:22:09,333 --> 00:22:10,375
I know.

297
00:22:11,460 --> 00:22:12,419
Bestie,

298
00:22:12,419 --> 00:22:13,587
Tripp has a point.

299
00:22:14,213 --> 00:22:16,089
He just hates seeing you sad.

300
00:22:18,050 --> 00:22:20,761
With Drake, it’s always one
problem after another.

301
00:22:21,929 --> 00:22:23,513
You know,

302
00:22:23,513 --> 00:22:25,182
I am Dralys all the way.

303
00:22:25,724 --> 00:22:27,726
But if you're not happy
with Drake anymore,

304
00:22:28,227 --> 00:22:29,853
you should start thinking about things.

305
00:22:30,187 --> 00:22:31,813
You can always run away.

306
00:22:32,105 --> 00:22:33,440
And you know that.

307
00:22:35,442 --> 00:22:36,735
But,

308
00:22:36,735 --> 00:22:39,112
how can true happiness be measured?

309
00:22:39,196 --> 00:22:42,074
Can it be measured by the
number of times that you smile?

310
00:22:43,075 --> 00:22:44,826
The laughter that you share?

311
00:22:45,994 --> 00:22:49,998
What's the true measure of happiness?

312
00:22:50,749 --> 00:22:52,251
Hang on.

313
00:22:53,085 --> 00:22:54,086
That's deep.

314
00:22:54,419 --> 00:22:56,588
I know in my heart that

315
00:22:58,298 --> 00:23:00,217
I'm happy with Drake.

316
00:23:00,968 --> 00:23:04,388
The memories that I cherish
the most are the ones with him.

317
00:23:05,347 --> 00:23:08,308
Every smile,

318
00:23:08,308 --> 00:23:11,520
every time he held my hand.

319
00:23:12,604 --> 00:23:14,273
I can’t bring myself to forget it.

320
00:23:15,315 --> 00:23:17,859
So even though he hurt
me so badly back then,

321
00:23:18,318 --> 00:23:21,780
it was just way too hard
for me to forget him.

322
00:23:23,407 --> 00:23:26,159
But when does too much become too much?

323
00:23:29,830 --> 00:23:30,914
Okay?

324
00:23:31,373 --> 00:23:33,041
That's enough.

325
00:23:34,293 --> 00:23:35,794
That's enough.

326
00:23:37,212 --> 00:23:38,714
I'm always here.

327
00:23:44,553 --> 00:23:46,179
What the hell?!

328
00:23:46,847 --> 00:23:48,098
What the fuck?!

329
00:23:49,099 --> 00:23:50,350
What's your problem?

330
00:23:57,316 --> 00:23:58,376
Nothing, I’m sorry.

331
00:24:03,822 --> 00:24:05,490
I’m confused too, Zy. I’m sorry.

332
00:24:09,077 --> 00:24:10,087
It’s just that...

333
00:24:12,247 --> 00:24:13,930
No matter how many times you hurt me,

334
00:24:15,520 --> 00:24:16,688
I still choose you.

335
00:24:20,172 --> 00:24:21,188
I’m sorry.

336
00:24:21,503 --> 00:24:23,442
The only thing I want
is to get on my knees,

337
00:24:23,467 --> 00:24:25,010
and beg for you to come back.

338
00:24:25,010 --> 00:24:26,428
Please come back to me, Zy.

339
00:24:26,428 --> 00:24:27,512
I don't know.

340
00:24:32,225 --> 00:24:33,619
After all these years, Zy.

341
00:24:36,055 --> 00:24:37,105
I just want to know...

342
00:24:37,860 --> 00:24:41,693
Did you ever feel, even once,
how much I loved you?

343
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:45,781
I love you so much.

344
00:24:46,239 --> 00:24:48,325
Even when I know you love Drake.

345
00:24:50,827 --> 00:24:53,955
Five fucking years, Zy.

346
00:24:54,966 --> 00:24:56,376
I gave you everything.

347
00:24:58,001 --> 00:24:59,628
All genuine effort.

348
00:25:01,922 --> 00:25:03,423
Even if it had to be in secret.

349
00:25:03,882 --> 00:25:05,550
Even if there’s someone
else to share you with.

350
00:25:08,095 --> 00:25:10,097
Even when forced, Zy.

351
00:25:11,556 --> 00:25:12,891
I gave you everything.

352
00:25:16,978 --> 00:25:17,938
You know what?

353
00:25:19,648 --> 00:25:23,693
Even if I look like an idiot
for everything I’ve been doing.

354
00:25:24,986 --> 00:25:26,405
I was at my happiest.

355
00:25:28,198 --> 00:25:29,157
I was happy with that.

356
00:25:31,743 --> 00:25:32,702
Zy.

357
00:25:34,746 --> 00:25:36,039
After all these years,

358
00:25:37,582 --> 00:25:39,876
I know I shouldn’t be saying this,

359
00:25:39,876 --> 00:25:41,878
but I don't even know if I deserve it, Zy.

360
00:25:42,272 --> 00:25:43,547
But please!

361
00:25:43,547 --> 00:25:45,507
Just hurt me! Please!

362
00:25:46,800 --> 00:25:47,759
Please...

363
00:25:48,176 --> 00:25:50,971
Please, Zy! Just do anything!

364
00:25:51,263 --> 00:25:52,806
Please hurt me!

365
00:25:53,515 --> 00:25:54,408
I can’t.

366
00:25:54,433 --> 00:25:55,659
I'm sorry.

367
00:25:55,684 --> 00:25:57,310
I don't know anymore, Zy.

368
00:25:57,436 --> 00:25:59,563
Break my heart, please do anything!

369
00:26:00,272 --> 00:26:01,815
Hurt me. Make me feel numb.

370
00:26:01,840 --> 00:26:03,717
That's the only thing I need, Zy,

371
00:26:04,234 --> 00:26:06,153
for me to finally move on!

372
00:26:06,153 --> 00:26:07,612
Because I don't know anymore!

373
00:26:07,679 --> 00:26:09,306
I'm sorry.

374
00:26:09,573 --> 00:26:10,949
I don't know anymore, Zy.

375
00:26:10,949 --> 00:26:12,093
I'm sorry.

376
00:26:12,200 --> 00:26:14,094
Tell me you never loved me!

377
00:26:14,119 --> 00:26:15,078
Zy!

378
00:26:15,078 --> 00:26:16,705
Tell me that you made a fool out of me!

379
00:26:16,830 --> 00:26:17,956
That's what I need, Zy!

380
00:26:17,956 --> 00:26:19,124
So, please!

381
00:26:24,546 --> 00:26:27,090
But when does too much become too much?

382
00:26:29,134 --> 00:26:30,886
I don't know, Bestie.

383
00:26:31,511 --> 00:26:33,263
All I know is,

384
00:26:34,514 --> 00:26:38,101
I feel like I lost a part
of myself when I lost him.

385
00:26:39,102 --> 00:26:41,897
Because he was a part of who I was.

386
00:26:42,481 --> 00:26:45,400
And honestly if I was given a chance,

387
00:26:45,425 --> 00:26:48,345
I would still like him to be
a part of who I would be.

388
00:26:54,868 --> 00:26:57,162
I know you understand, Bestie.

389
00:26:57,579 --> 00:27:00,207
That's why you're entertaining Kent again.

390
00:27:00,916 --> 00:27:02,017
My goodness.

391
00:27:02,042 --> 00:27:04,127
Why are we talking about me now?

392
00:27:09,799 --> 00:27:12,177
With Drake, everything just seems hopeful.

393
00:27:14,012 --> 00:27:15,639
Ever since I met him.

394
00:27:16,056 --> 00:27:18,683
I always look forward
to tomorrow because

395
00:27:18,892 --> 00:27:21,061
I know that it will all be worth it.

396
00:27:23,730 --> 00:27:25,899
Don't worry, Bestie.

397
00:27:25,899 --> 00:27:27,567
Everything will be alright.

398
00:27:28,276 --> 00:27:29,945
I hope so.

399
00:27:29,945 --> 00:27:31,738
I hope so, Bestie.

400
00:27:32,447 --> 00:27:36,201
Because I'm having such
a hard time with everything.

401
00:27:36,201 --> 00:27:38,745
I feel like anytime I'll just

402
00:27:38,745 --> 00:27:40,288
explode.

403
00:27:40,747 --> 00:27:43,833
I feel like everything
will like crash and burn.

404
00:27:45,460 --> 00:27:46,795
Bestie,

405
00:27:46,820 --> 00:27:49,864
I know you're having such a hard time.

406
00:27:50,757 --> 00:27:53,677
I see how much you're
fighting even if it's hard.

407
00:27:55,971 --> 00:27:59,307
But remember, Bestie.

408
00:28:00,684 --> 00:28:03,103
You don't have to do
this all on your own.

409
00:28:03,603 --> 00:28:05,397
I'm here.

410
00:28:05,981 --> 00:28:08,108
I'm always here for you.

411
00:28:11,444 --> 00:28:13,446
Thank you, Bestie.

412
00:28:14,371 --> 00:28:16,401
I'm tired, Bestie.

413
00:28:18,201 --> 00:28:19,573
Bestie,

414
00:28:20,647 --> 00:28:22,120
It's okay to be tired.

415
00:28:22,847 --> 00:28:24,269
It's okay to cry.

416
00:28:24,749 --> 00:28:27,379
It doesn't mean you're weak.

417
00:28:28,128 --> 00:28:30,005
All it means is

418
00:28:30,005 --> 00:28:30,922
you're human.

419
00:28:30,922 --> 00:28:32,507
You can get hurt,

420
00:28:32,507 --> 00:28:34,092
or get tired.

421
00:28:36,720 --> 00:28:38,088
I know you, Bestie.

422
00:28:38,597 --> 00:28:40,223
You're a strong woman.

423
00:28:40,932 --> 00:28:43,643
You've been through so much.

424
00:28:44,249 --> 00:28:45,401
And I know,

425
00:28:46,354 --> 00:28:47,940
you'll get through this.

426
00:28:51,276 --> 00:28:52,456
Thank you, Bestie.

427
00:28:57,407 --> 00:28:58,742
Love you, Bestie.

428
00:29:00,619 --> 00:29:01,953
Love you, Bestie.

429
00:29:02,377 --> 00:29:03,879
Crazy & Ugly!

430
00:29:04,456 --> 00:29:05,749
Crazy Aya!

431
00:29:06,913 --> 00:29:10,250
Ugly Alys!

432
00:29:42,160 --> 00:29:45,163
Why did I even wake up?

433
00:29:46,956 --> 00:29:49,417
Here I go again.

434
00:29:50,543 --> 00:29:55,173
I have to face this complicated
reality with Drake.

435
00:29:56,549 --> 00:29:58,693
And then there's Tripp too.

436
00:30:20,490 --> 00:30:22,617
I haven't heard from you since yesterday.

437
00:30:22,617 --> 00:30:25,245
Are you really not going
to reach out today either?

438
00:30:25,662 --> 00:30:28,456
What's taking you so long?

439
00:30:41,136 --> 00:30:43,722
Drake, I know you're
going through a lot.

440
00:30:43,722 --> 00:30:46,349
But please don't spiral.

441
00:30:49,936 --> 00:30:51,013
Drake!

442
00:30:51,563 --> 00:30:52,693
Yes?

443
00:30:56,943 --> 00:30:57,919
How—

444
00:30:59,279 --> 00:31:00,905
Have you eaten?

445
00:31:00,905 --> 00:31:02,073
Not yet.

446
00:31:02,073 --> 00:31:03,700
Let's have lunch together.

447
00:31:04,743 --> 00:31:06,911
Good thing he still remembers me.

448
00:31:07,495 --> 00:31:09,748
I thought he’d always be down.

449
00:31:11,499 --> 00:31:12,333
Alright.

450
00:31:12,709 --> 00:31:14,210
I'll come see you later.

451
00:31:14,502 --> 00:31:16,004
I'll come get you instead.

452
00:31:17,464 --> 00:31:19,758
No, it's fine. I can go to you.

453
00:31:20,049 --> 00:31:21,092
Okay.

454
00:31:23,386 --> 00:31:24,429
Drake?

455
00:31:26,681 --> 00:31:27,943
I love you so much.

456
00:31:29,893 --> 00:31:31,186
Always and forever.

457
00:31:32,896 --> 00:31:34,189
To the moon and back.

458
00:31:45,074 --> 00:31:46,706
I love you too, my wife.

459
00:32:12,060 --> 00:32:14,312
Breakfast delivery!

460
00:32:17,440 --> 00:32:18,650
With no delivery charge.

461
00:32:18,650 --> 00:32:19,734
Just a smile,

462
00:32:19,734 --> 00:32:20,816
and you're all set.

463
00:32:21,528 --> 00:32:23,071
Good morning, Bee.

464
00:32:23,947 --> 00:32:25,240
You're early.

465
00:32:26,241 --> 00:32:28,326
Bee, you're forgetting to eat again.

466
00:32:28,326 --> 00:32:29,702
That's bad.

467
00:32:31,496 --> 00:32:33,456
One, two, three, four...

468
00:32:34,415 --> 00:32:37,335
And how are you so sure
I haven't had breakfast?

469
00:32:37,794 --> 00:32:39,921
Do you have psychic powers now?

470
00:32:41,464 --> 00:32:42,715
Your mom said so.

471
00:32:45,385 --> 00:32:46,553
For you!

472
00:32:48,721 --> 00:32:49,889
Steamed bun,

473
00:32:50,890 --> 00:32:52,058
and...

474
00:32:52,058 --> 00:32:53,226
All I know is,

475
00:32:54,769 --> 00:32:57,981
I feel like I lost a part
of myself when I lost him.

476
00:32:59,315 --> 00:33:01,734
Because he was a part of who I was.

477
00:33:05,280 --> 00:33:07,198
There it is!

478
00:33:09,158 --> 00:33:10,285
Bee needs to eat.

479
00:33:15,957 --> 00:33:17,208
Kent...

480
00:33:17,208 --> 00:33:18,001
Bee?

481
00:33:19,711 --> 00:33:21,963
Thank you for your efforts.

482
00:33:25,925 --> 00:33:27,802
But what if,

483
00:33:29,971 --> 00:33:31,514
we don't get back together?

484
00:33:43,693 --> 00:33:45,945
I'd be sad.

485
00:33:53,661 --> 00:33:55,538
But I'd understand.

486
00:33:59,459 --> 00:34:03,254
I won't force it if you don't want me.

487
00:34:07,717 --> 00:34:11,012
Like they say,

488
00:34:11,012 --> 00:34:14,599
it's better to be loved
when you’re chosen,

489
00:34:14,599 --> 00:34:16,643
not when you’re forced to it.

490
00:34:23,566 --> 00:34:25,944
Come on, eat up.

491
00:34:27,278 --> 00:34:29,238
Even if you forget about me.

492
00:34:30,490 --> 00:34:31,950
Even if you don’t choose me.

493
00:34:34,077 --> 00:34:37,121
As long as you choose
to take care of yourself.

494
00:34:39,707 --> 00:34:40,792
Okay?

495
00:34:50,760 --> 00:34:51,678
Bee.

496
00:34:52,512 --> 00:34:53,304
Bee?

497
00:34:54,806 --> 00:34:56,557
Did you call me “Bee”?

498
00:34:59,018 --> 00:35:00,812
Why are you leaving?

499
00:35:01,437 --> 00:35:02,939
Did I ever say

500
00:35:02,939 --> 00:35:04,315
that I wasn't choosing you?

501
00:35:05,191 --> 00:35:06,275
Did I ever say

502
00:35:06,275 --> 00:35:07,944
that I wanted to forget about you?

503
00:35:08,486 --> 00:35:09,570
Bee, hold on.

504
00:35:11,322 --> 00:35:12,532
What are you saying?

505
00:35:12,991 --> 00:35:13,992
Are we back together?

506
00:35:18,538 --> 00:35:20,707
Yes! Bee!

507
00:35:24,002 --> 00:35:25,461
Bee...

508
00:35:26,212 --> 00:35:27,672
Can I hug you?

509
00:35:31,009 --> 00:35:33,302
Bee, I missed you so much, Bee!

510
00:35:33,845 --> 00:35:35,888
I have one condition, though.

511
00:35:36,431 --> 00:35:37,557
What is it?

512
00:35:37,765 --> 00:35:39,934
I don't want you to be super clingy.

513
00:35:40,393 --> 00:35:41,728
Just a little bit.

514
00:35:44,647 --> 00:35:45,606
Alright, Bee.

515
00:35:45,853 --> 00:35:46,812
I promise.

516
00:36:03,833 --> 00:36:06,085
Alys, it's just a normal day.

517
00:36:06,085 --> 00:36:08,212
You're not running away
from the problem.

518
00:36:08,212 --> 00:36:10,381
You just want a break.

519
00:36:23,603 --> 00:36:25,480
Mommy?

520
00:36:27,607 --> 00:36:29,108
Dear?

521
00:36:29,484 --> 00:36:30,610
Yes, Mommy?

522
00:36:30,610 --> 00:36:31,611
What is it?

523
00:36:32,403 --> 00:36:35,114
Tripp came by the house earlier.

524
00:36:35,448 --> 00:36:36,574
Huh?

525
00:36:37,075 --> 00:36:39,911
And I told him you're
gonna be in the condo so

526
00:36:39,911 --> 00:36:41,245
he may be coming.

527
00:36:43,623 --> 00:36:45,166
Alys?

528
00:36:45,166 --> 00:36:47,085
You know, I love you so much.

529
00:36:47,376 --> 00:36:50,463
And I'm always behind you in
every decision that you make.

530
00:36:50,755 --> 00:36:54,092
But please put yourself first.

531
00:36:54,383 --> 00:36:55,301
Okay?

532
00:36:55,593 --> 00:36:57,053
Just because you love someone

533
00:36:57,053 --> 00:37:00,598
it doesn't give you the license to
hurt yourself over and over again.

534
00:37:00,598 --> 00:37:01,532
Okay?

535
00:37:01,557 --> 00:37:03,810
Because if that's the case,

536
00:37:03,810 --> 00:37:05,353
that's not love anymore.

537
00:37:07,063 --> 00:37:08,856
It's just a responsibility.

538
00:37:08,856 --> 00:37:11,484
And remember that love is bliss,

539
00:37:11,484 --> 00:37:12,652
and not ignorance.

540
00:37:12,652 --> 00:37:13,694
Okay?

541
00:37:14,237 --> 00:37:15,279
Thanks, Mom.

542
00:37:16,155 --> 00:37:17,865
Love you, Baby!

543
00:37:17,865 --> 00:37:19,325
Always remember that.

544
00:37:19,826 --> 00:37:20,993
Of course, Mom.

545
00:37:20,993 --> 00:37:22,056
I love you, too.

546
00:37:22,537 --> 00:37:23,540
Bye.

547
00:37:23,663 --> 00:37:24,831
Bye.

548
00:37:25,556 --> 00:37:27,500
Mom, I know you meant well.

549
00:37:27,525 --> 00:37:31,126
But I'd rather be ignorant with Drake

550
00:37:31,420 --> 00:37:32,880
than to be smart and alone.

551
00:37:53,151 --> 00:37:53,901
Zy...

552
00:37:55,486 --> 00:37:57,113
What are you doing here?

553
00:37:59,866 --> 00:38:00,700
Well...

554
00:38:01,617 --> 00:38:02,702
Can we talk?

555
00:38:04,537 --> 00:38:06,497
I thought I was supposed
to stay away from you?

556
00:38:06,706 --> 00:38:08,040
Zy...

557
00:38:08,875 --> 00:38:10,209
Tripp, please.

558
00:38:13,462 --> 00:38:15,381
You asked me to stay away, right?

559
00:38:16,048 --> 00:38:17,633
Then cooperate with me.

560
00:38:23,097 --> 00:38:24,348
Zy,

561
00:38:25,516 --> 00:38:27,101
this is the last one.

562
00:38:28,352 --> 00:38:29,937
I just

563
00:38:31,105 --> 00:38:33,900
really wanted to see you
for one last time.

564
00:38:35,693 --> 00:38:37,278
After this...

565
00:38:39,322 --> 00:38:40,865
I'm leaving.

566
00:38:42,450 --> 00:38:43,993
He's leaving?

567
00:38:45,036 --> 00:38:46,579
Why does it hurt?

568
00:38:47,830 --> 00:38:50,458
I know I have to stay away.

569
00:38:50,833 --> 00:38:53,461
But why does he have to leave?

570
00:38:54,170 --> 00:38:55,171
Why?

571
00:38:56,380 --> 00:38:57,798
Where are you going?

572
00:39:03,804 --> 00:39:04,972
I can't say.

573
00:39:07,975 --> 00:39:09,143
Somewhere far.

574
00:39:12,313 --> 00:39:14,690
Wherever there's

575
00:39:14,690 --> 00:39:17,401
no Alys Zyril Perez.

576
00:39:21,447 --> 00:39:23,699
I just want to start over.

577
00:39:25,826 --> 00:39:28,871
I want to find someone

578
00:39:29,580 --> 00:39:31,415
who will love me.

579
00:39:33,125 --> 00:39:34,710
For real.

580
00:39:40,258 --> 00:39:42,301
I want to know how it feels

581
00:39:43,511 --> 00:39:45,179
to be chosen.

582
00:39:49,892 --> 00:39:51,560
Tripp, I'm so sorry.

583
00:39:58,484 --> 00:39:59,802
You don't have to be.

584
00:40:02,571 --> 00:40:04,240
I’m the one who fell in love with you.

585
00:40:24,407 --> 00:40:25,366
Hello?

586
00:40:25,862 --> 00:40:28,490
Alys, Fier is leaving!

587
00:40:28,764 --> 00:40:31,183
My conscience can't
take not telling you.

588
00:40:31,851 --> 00:40:33,060
What?

589
00:40:34,145 --> 00:40:35,730
Where is Fier going?

590
00:40:36,487 --> 00:40:37,989
She said she’s going abroad.

591
00:40:38,357 --> 00:40:40,818
She's going somewhere
far away with their baby.

592
00:40:40,818 --> 00:40:42,194
But that's unfair!

593
00:40:42,194 --> 00:40:43,821
Alys, hurry, please!

594
00:40:43,821 --> 00:40:44,947
Go to her now.

595
00:40:44,947 --> 00:40:45,948
Her flight is tonight.

596
00:40:45,948 --> 00:40:47,575
Her flight is tonight?!

597
00:40:52,288 --> 00:40:53,111
Hey.

598
00:40:53,456 --> 00:40:54,439
What happened?

599
00:40:54,498 --> 00:40:55,166
I need to go.

600
00:40:55,166 --> 00:40:57,668
I have to stop Fier before she leaves.

601
00:40:59,337 --> 00:41:00,173
Let's go.

602
00:41:01,213 --> 00:41:02,631
I’ll help you with your problem.

603
00:41:04,592 --> 00:41:06,010
Before I leave.

604
00:41:15,728 --> 00:41:16,687
For one last time.

605
00:41:28,964 --> 00:41:31,175
Zy? What's wrong?

606
00:41:31,994 --> 00:41:34,121
I'm not sure I can do this, Tripp.

607
00:41:36,165 --> 00:41:37,708
You have to be strong.

608
00:41:38,757 --> 00:41:40,801
Don't you want to fix things?

609
00:41:42,755 --> 00:41:43,923
When are you going to face them?

610
00:41:45,132 --> 00:41:46,300
But —

611
00:41:46,300 --> 00:41:48,761
No, Zy. You can do this!

612
00:41:48,962 --> 00:41:50,672
I believe you can do this.

613
00:41:51,764 --> 00:41:53,057
Don't worry, okay?

614
00:41:54,568 --> 00:41:56,528
After this,

615
00:41:57,603 --> 00:41:59,105
I'll be gone, too.

616
00:42:03,859 --> 00:42:05,694
But before that happens,

617
00:42:05,694 --> 00:42:07,780
I want you to promise me one thing.

618
00:42:09,698 --> 00:42:13,035
Never feel ashamed
to cry in front of Drake.

619
00:42:14,370 --> 00:42:15,746
You know why?

620
00:42:17,832 --> 00:42:19,875
When someone truly loves you,

621
00:42:20,876 --> 00:42:22,294
they'll understand you.

622
00:42:23,254 --> 00:42:25,506
Whether you’re crying or laughing.

623
00:42:26,674 --> 00:42:27,842
As for Drake?

624
00:42:30,052 --> 00:42:31,679
He loves you so much.

625
00:42:32,805 --> 00:42:33,639
Okay?

626
00:42:38,185 --> 00:42:40,896
Thank you for understanding me, Tripp.

627
00:42:42,982 --> 00:42:44,984
Everything will be alright, okay?

628
00:42:45,609 --> 00:42:47,069
For you.

629
00:42:47,528 --> 00:42:49,113
For me.

630
00:42:50,156 --> 00:42:51,073
For everyone.

631
00:42:52,741 --> 00:42:53,451
Go.

632
00:42:53,784 --> 00:42:54,493
You can do this.

633
00:42:55,035 --> 00:42:56,287
I'll be here, okay?

634
00:42:57,746 --> 00:42:58,998
You've got this, Zy.

635
00:43:18,559 --> 00:43:19,477
Just chill, okay?

636
00:43:19,477 --> 00:43:20,352
-Cris—
-Relax.

637
00:43:21,437 --> 00:43:23,063
Stop following me!

638
00:43:23,063 --> 00:43:26,066
I'm leaving even if you
cry or beg on your knees.

639
00:43:27,109 --> 00:43:29,278
Fier, don't do this to me.

640
00:43:31,447 --> 00:43:33,324
Your chance is over, Drake.

641
00:43:33,324 --> 00:43:34,450
I'm done with you.

642
00:43:35,576 --> 00:43:37,620
Sure.
At some point,

643
00:43:37,620 --> 00:43:40,080
I may have thought I fell for you.

644
00:43:41,499 --> 00:43:42,708
But you hurt me.

645
00:43:44,543 --> 00:43:46,462
And when people hurt me,

646
00:43:46,462 --> 00:43:47,379
I'm done.

647
00:43:47,379 --> 00:43:48,214
Game over.

648
00:43:49,131 --> 00:43:50,674
Sorry but that's how I roll.

649
00:43:51,717 --> 00:43:53,093
Where are you going, Fier?

650
00:43:53,093 --> 00:43:54,720
Would you please tell me?

651
00:43:55,554 --> 00:43:57,473
You have no right to know, okay?

652
00:43:58,057 --> 00:44:00,184
Don't act like a responsible father.

653
00:44:01,560 --> 00:44:02,857
Fier, please.

654
00:44:04,396 --> 00:44:05,427
Fier!

655
00:44:06,325 --> 00:44:07,242
Please!

656
00:44:07,858 --> 00:44:08,776
Please!

657
00:44:10,069 --> 00:44:10,986
Please!

658
00:44:12,279 --> 00:44:13,280
You've made your choice.

659
00:44:13,438 --> 00:44:14,648
You chose Alys.

660
00:44:14,782 --> 00:44:15,950
Fier, please!

661
00:44:16,277 --> 00:44:19,489
- Fier!
- You don't have business with me,

662
00:44:19,513 --> 00:44:20,514
or my child.

663
00:44:21,789 --> 00:44:22,831
Please, Fier!

664
00:44:25,626 --> 00:44:26,546
Fier!

665
00:44:26,877 --> 00:44:27,836
Why, Drake?

666
00:44:28,546 --> 00:44:30,756
Why are you doing this to yourself?

667
00:44:31,507 --> 00:44:33,384
Stop begging.

668
00:44:33,884 --> 00:44:35,386
I know.

669
00:44:35,386 --> 00:44:37,304
I understand you and Alys.

670
00:44:37,930 --> 00:44:39,890
You love each other.

671
00:44:40,856 --> 00:44:41,983
Fier.

672
00:44:42,893 --> 00:44:45,145
So don't worry, okay?

673
00:44:46,355 --> 00:44:49,108
I'll take good care of our child.

674
00:44:51,026 --> 00:44:53,237
I'll make sure she has a good life.

675
00:44:54,321 --> 00:44:55,239
Please...

676
00:44:55,864 --> 00:44:58,075
Don't take my child away from me.

677
00:45:00,869 --> 00:45:02,037
I can't stay.

678
00:45:02,538 --> 00:45:05,082
Don't take our child away from me, Fier.

679
00:45:05,416 --> 00:45:08,252
I'd just hurt myself every day.

680
00:45:08,419 --> 00:45:09,712
Please, Fier.

681
00:45:09,712 --> 00:45:12,548
Don't do this to me, please.

682
00:45:12,548 --> 00:45:13,591
Fier.

683
00:45:14,466 --> 00:45:17,428
Don't keep my child from me.

684
00:45:20,139 --> 00:45:21,849
I'll fix this, Fier.

685
00:45:21,849 --> 00:45:23,309
Help me.

686
00:45:26,604 --> 00:45:27,616
Fier.

687
00:45:29,231 --> 00:45:30,608
Sorry, but I have to say goodbye.

688
00:45:30,608 --> 00:45:32,192
- Fier.
- I’m sorry. No.

689
00:45:32,443 --> 00:45:33,569
Fier!

690
00:45:37,615 --> 00:45:38,741
Fier.

691
00:45:56,508 --> 00:45:57,676
Hey!

692
00:45:58,135 --> 00:45:59,094
Zy?

693
00:45:59,613 --> 00:46:00,727
What happened?

694
00:46:02,640 --> 00:46:04,850
- Tripp!
- Tell me.

695
00:46:04,912 --> 00:46:06,247
- Tripp!
- What happened?

696
00:46:08,102 --> 00:46:09,604
Give me the keys!

697
00:46:09,772 --> 00:46:10,439
You can't drive like this—

698
00:46:10,439 --> 00:46:12,816
I said, give me the fucking keys!

699
00:46:21,241 --> 00:46:22,242
Zy!

700
00:46:24,960 --> 00:46:27,650
Tripp, please I want to be alone!

701
00:46:28,499 --> 00:46:29,667
You shouldn’t drive like this—

702
00:46:29,667 --> 00:46:32,454
I said I want to be alone!

703
00:46:33,128 --> 00:46:36,215
Is that so hard to understand, Tripp?

704
00:46:36,215 --> 00:46:37,925
Just leave me alone.

705
00:46:38,676 --> 00:46:39,426
Alright.

706
00:46:40,594 --> 00:46:41,762
Fine, then drive.

707
00:46:41,787 --> 00:46:42,913
I’m just here.

708
00:46:58,320 --> 00:46:59,197
Zy.

709
00:47:02,491 --> 00:47:03,325
Zy.

710
00:47:04,243 --> 00:47:05,173
Slow down.

711
00:47:05,198 --> 00:47:06,118
Please!

712
00:47:07,538 --> 00:47:08,080
Zy, please.

713
00:47:08,080 --> 00:47:09,206
You're going over the speed limit!

714
00:47:09,206 --> 00:47:10,057
Zy, please.

715
00:47:10,082 --> 00:47:11,875
I don't care!

716
00:47:11,875 --> 00:47:13,252
I don't care!

717
00:47:13,252 --> 00:47:14,211
Zy, please!

718
00:47:14,275 --> 00:47:15,318
Steady!

719
00:47:15,343 --> 00:47:17,053
You're losing control! Please!

720
00:47:17,464 --> 00:47:18,330
Zy!

721
00:47:21,719 --> 00:47:22,778
Zy!

722
00:47:22,803 --> 00:47:23,923
Please, listen to me!

723
00:47:24,388 --> 00:47:26,432
If you have a problem,
we can talk about it, please!

724
00:47:26,432 --> 00:47:28,434
Just stop the car Zy, please!

725
00:48:07,723 --> 00:48:09,349
Tripp...

726
00:48:24,823 --> 00:48:27,826
Oh my god.
No, please!

727
00:48:30,662 --> 00:48:31,428
Tripp!

728
00:48:31,852 --> 00:48:32,614
Tripp!

729
00:48:33,165 --> 00:48:33,974
Tripp!

730
00:48:33,999 --> 00:48:35,292
Tripp, wake up. Please!

731
00:48:37,586 --> 00:48:39,379
Help!

732
00:48:40,963 --> 00:48:42,020
Help!

733
00:48:42,355 --> 00:48:44,023
Help!

734
00:48:49,139 --> 00:48:51,350
Help!

735
00:49:32,020 --> 00:49:33,051
Hop on.

736
00:49:37,314 --> 00:49:38,774
By the way, Zy, I'm taking you home.

737
00:49:39,273 --> 00:49:40,399
Okay!

738
00:49:45,320 --> 00:49:48,031
I’m still waiting for the woman
who makes my heart race.

739
00:49:50,784 --> 00:49:52,995
You love Alys, right?

740
00:49:54,329 --> 00:49:55,333
So much.

741
00:50:23,297 --> 00:50:24,131
Relax,

742
00:50:24,330 --> 00:50:26,207
I'm just trying to make you laugh.

743
00:50:33,827 --> 00:50:35,871
Tripp, thank you.

744
00:50:42,353 --> 00:50:44,397
I hope you’ll always be by my side.

745
00:50:47,154 --> 00:50:49,198
You never leave me.

746
00:50:52,327 --> 00:50:53,510
Not yet.

747
00:50:53,597 --> 00:50:54,932
I still can’t.

748
00:50:54,932 --> 00:50:56,266
What?

749
00:50:56,808 --> 00:50:57,874
Nothing.

750
00:51:09,446 --> 00:51:13,659
Zy, I love you so much.

751
00:51:21,971 --> 00:51:22,781
Tripp.

752
00:51:23,251 --> 00:51:24,173
Tripp?

753
00:51:24,546 --> 00:51:26,672
Alys was with Tripp when it happened.

754
00:51:27,373 --> 00:51:28,332
Tripp.

755
00:51:35,138 --> 00:51:37,057
Alys, I’m here. I won’t leave you.

756
00:51:37,057 --> 00:51:38,684
Drake, where is Tripp?

757
00:51:39,220 --> 00:51:42,014
I'm just happy that Alys is alive.

758
00:51:42,155 --> 00:51:43,198
Even though—

759
00:51:44,316 --> 00:51:45,192
Hey, Bestie!

760
00:51:45,707 --> 00:51:46,959
You need to eat, Alys.

761
00:51:46,984 --> 00:51:48,986
Where's Tripp? I want to see him.

762
00:51:50,287 --> 00:51:51,445
Come on, Alys.

763
00:51:51,709 --> 00:51:53,140
I want to see Tripp!

764
00:51:53,165 --> 00:51:54,547
Are you deaf or what?
